{
  "$comment": [
    "What we expect the openagents.com web chat to do when people ask what they actually ask (docs/web/chat-goldens.md). Each golden is one expectation; each phrasing is one case sent through the same path the live site uses.",
    "route: the chat router routes that are right (any one). answers: the prepared answer or product note ids whose text is right (any one; a bank id without @version, a note id like openagents.github-projects). An empty list means any served answer, or none, is fine.",
    "tier: the served tier words that are right. Product notes served whole come back as tier canned with the note id as the answer. speed: instant (Jev picks a prepared answer or note, shown at once) or model (the chat model writes it).",
    "required: each item is a list of alternatives; one of them must appear in the reply, case-insensitive. forbidden: none may appear. Every reply is also checked against the set's forbidden list and for machine talk (oa-copy).",
    "Secrets in phrasings are fake placeholders, never real keys.",
    "Do not tune bank `when` text or note `applies_when` text against these phrasings one by one; they are the expectations, not training data. Fix the product knowledge when a golden is right and the reply is wrong."
  ],
  "schema": "openagents.web-chat.goldens.v1",
  "set": "web-chat-goldens-v1",
  "created": "2026-10-09",
  "surface": "web",
  "budgets": {
    "instant": { "first_ms": 3000, "total_ms": 3500, "judge_ms": 2000 },
    "model": { "first_ms": 10000, "total_ms": 60000, "judge_ms": 2000 }
  },
  "forbidden": [
    "we don't train on",
    "we do not train on",
    "we never train on",
    "we won't train on",
    "don't use your chats to train",
    "don't use your conversations to train",
    "there's no account",
    "there is no account",
    "OpenAgents for Mac 1.0",
    ".dmg",
    "computer you've connected",
    "As an AI language model",
    "Project map",
    "Code finder",
    "Test reader",
    "Explain this error"
  ],
  "gate": {
    "$comment": "The launch bar (#11106): a whole-set run exits 1 below it. min_right is the share of cases that must be right: passing, or right but slow (over a time budget, or written by the model instead of a prepared answer shown whole, with every text check passing). critical: flows and goldens where no case may be wrong: the four questions under the chat box, what models we use, how-tos (install Coder, sign Coder in, sync, connect a computer, connect a repository), pricing and plans, and privacy and training.",
    "min_right": 0.9,
    "critical": [
      "starters",
      "about.model",
      "coder.install",
      "coder.login",
      "coder.sync",
      "account.connect_computer",
      "github.connect_repo",
      "pricing",
      "privacy"
    ]
  },
